assets/blocks_1211.json
-----------------------
Block data for Minecraft Java 1.21.1, byte-identical to
`data/pc/1.21.1/blocks.json` in https://github.com/PrismarineJS/minecraft-data
(last changed upstream in commit d56346a4e32defcd28d9ba6750957c12001e78d6).

minecraft-data is distributed under the MIT license ("License: MIT" in its README). The
upstream repository has no LICENSE file and no named copyright holder at the time of
writing, so none is reproduced here. The upstream README also notes that some of the data
was extracted from wiki.vg and minecraft.gamepedia.com.

Minecraft data (development checkout versus public export)
---------------------------------------------------------
Derived from Minecraft, (c) Mojang Studios / Microsoft; not covered by megu's LGPL-3.0-or-later
license. Do not redistribute these outputs or the jar. The development
branch tracks datapacks/vanilla/, assets/block_states_1211.json, config_packets.bin,
tests/data/biome_probe_ties_1211.tsv and tests/data/random_next_int_1211.tsv.
tools/vanilla_data/gen_vanilla_data.sh generates these and tests/data/biome_probe_1211.tsv
and tests/data/vanilla_vectors_1211.tsv from the user's own 1.21.1 server jar
(sha1 59353fb40c36d304f2035d51e7d6e6baa98dc05c). Capturing config_packets.bin
requires the user's explicit --accept-eula. --verify checks the datapack without a jar.
tools/export_public_branch.sh omits all these paths and ignores local regenerated copies
in a new repository with no development history. Passing its audit is not release clearance.

Tool inputs that are not distributed
------------------------------------
tools/vanilla_data/ resolves obfuscated names with Fabric's intermediary (1.21.1) and Yarn
(1.21.1+build.3) mappings, both published under CC0-1.0 by FabricMC. They are downloaded
by the user when regenerating and are not part of this repository.

JVM-side components (fetched at build/run time, not distributed)
----------------------------------------------------------------
compat/*/build.py download the following, pinned by URL and SHA-256 in compat/*/dependencies.json,
into git-ignored .cache/ directories. No jar, class file or source of these is committed here,
and megu does not redistribute them. They keep their own licenses (as declared by the
upstream projects; check the downloaded artifacts before redistributing any of them):
  Fabric Loader 0.19.5 (Apache-2.0, FabricMC); SpongePowered Mixin 0.17.4 as built by FabricMC
  (MIT); ASM 9.10.1 (BSD-3-Clause); NeoForge 21.1.172, NeoForged event bus 8.0.2, FancyModLoader
  4.0.39 and MergeTool 2.0.0 (LGPL-2.1); log4j-api 2.23.1, JetBrains annotations 24.1.0 and
  typetools 0.6.3 (Apache-2.0).
The pinned third-party test mod (Seed Protect 1.0.0 by Itamio, from Modrinth) is used only as a
test input and is not distributed here; its jar metadata says "All Rights Reserved" while its
Modrinth page says MIT, so do not redistribute it.
The Java sources under compat/ are megu's own code. The classes under compat/*/java/net/minecraft/
are empty placeholder shapes (a name only, no Minecraft code) that satisfy method signatures.
